Assignment: Deploying and Networking Ubuntu Server 22.04
Background
In this lab, we will transition from IT theory to real-world operations by building a fully functional server from scratch. You will use VirtualBox to provision hardware, install a headless Linux operating system, and configure a dual-NIC (Network Interface Card) setup. You will use one adapter for internet access and configure a static IP on the second adapter to create a secure, private management network between your laptop and the server.

Objectives
By the end of this assignment, you should be able to:

Provision virtual hardware resources for a new virtual server.

Configure a Dual-NIC setup using NAT and Host-Only networking.

Perform a manual installation of a headless server operating system.

Identify multiple network adapters and configure them using Netplan.

Verify network connectivity by remotely connecting to the server via SSH.

Instructions
Initialize the Virtual Machine

Open VirtualBox.

Click Machine > New from the top menu.

In the Name field, type ServerLab-01-[YourInitials].

Set the Type dropdown to Linux.

Set the Version dropdown to Ubuntu (64-bit).

Important: Check the box that says Skip Unattended Installation.

Click Next.

Allocate Resources

Set Base Memory to 2048 MB.

Set Processors to 2.

Click Next.

Select Create a Virtual Hard Disk Now.

Set the disk size to 20.00 GB.

Click Next, then click Finish.

Configure the Dual Network Adapters

Right-click your new VM in the left menu and select Settings.

Click on the Network tab.

Adapter 1: Ensure "Enable Network Adapter" is checked and "Attached to" is set to NAT. (This provides internet access).

Click the Adapter 2 tab at the top.

Check Enable Network Adapter.

Change "Attached to" to Host-Only Adapter. (This creates our private management network for SSH).

Click OK.

Mount the ISO and Boot

Go to Settings > Storage.

Under "Controller: IDE", click the CD icon labeled Empty.

On the far right side of the window, click the small blue disk icon.

Choose Choose a disk file....

Select the ubuntu-server-22.04.iso file provided in class.

Click the green Start arrow to boot the VM.

Install the OS

Use your arrow keys to select Try or Install Ubuntu Server and press Enter.

Proceed through the installer using these exact settings (leave any unmentioned screens as default and select Done):

Language/Keyboard: English

Network: You will see two interfaces. Leave both as DHCP for now.

Storage: Check "Use an entire disk", then confirm the destructive formatting when prompted.

Profile Setup: Name: Class Admin | Server Name: srv-core-01 | Username: sysadmin | Password: Password123!

Ubuntu Pro: Select "Skip for now".

SSH Setup: Press the Spacebar to check "Install OpenSSH server".

Featured Snaps: Leave all unchecked.

Wait for the "Install complete!" message at the bottom of the screen.

Select Reboot Now (press Enter if prompted to remove the installation media).

Identify Your Network Adapters

Once the server reboots, log in with username sysadmin and password Password123!.

Type ip a and press Enter.

Look at the output. You will see two active network adapters (usually named enp0s3 and enp0s8).

The first one (enp0s3) will have a 10.0.x.x IP address from the NAT connection. The second one (enp0s8) is your Host-Only adapter. Write down the name of the second adapter.




Configure the Static IP

Type sudo nano /etc/netplan/00-installer-config.yaml and press Enter.

Edit the file to configure both adapters.

CRITICAL: Do NOT use the Tab key. Use the Spacebar to create indents.

Replace [ADAPTER_2_NAME] with your second adapter name (e.g., enp0s8). Replace [SEAT_NUMBER] with your physical seat number in the classroom.

YAML
network:
  ethernets:
    enp0s3:
      dhcp4: true
    [ADAPTER_2_NAME]:
      dhcp4: false
      addresses: [192.168.56.[SEAT_NUMBER]/24]
  version: 2

Note: We do not put a gateway on Adapter 2, because we want internet traffic to continue flowing out of Adapter 1.

Press Ctrl+O then Enter to save the file.

Press Ctrl+X to exit the text editor.

Type sudo netplan apply and press Enter to push the configuration.

Verify Connectivity

Minimize the VirtualBox window.

Open Command Prompt (Windows) or Terminal (macOS) on your physical host computer.

Type ssh sysadmin@192.168.56.[SEAT_NUMBER] (using the static IP you just assigned).

Press Enter.

Type yes to accept the security fingerprint.

Enter your password. You are now remotely managing your server over your private Host-Only network!

